description: Mitzo staging and its pipeline are stood down; use offline tests, review and CI
alwaysApply: true
---

Canonical Mitzo staging and its pipeline on this Mac are stood down as of
15 October 2026. Do not run staging checks, enqueue post-merge work, deploy,
recover, restart or recreate staging as part of ordinary Mitzo work.

The former `http://mitzo-staging.localhost:3190`, `com.mitzo.staging` and
`~/.local/share/mitzo-staging` are historical references. Repository staging
procedures are historical; reactivation requires a new explicit user request.
Preserve retained ownership, operation and diagnostic records, including
Symposium ownership and retained October checkpoints.

Use offline tests, review and CI. Live testing requires a separately selected
and authorized target. Do not borrow production credentials/configuration or
use production as an automatic test fallback. Production ports 3100/3101 and
its releases/job remain excluded from staging operations. Production deployment
requires a separate explicit user action.

Real model tests must explicitly use a supported Luna model and announce the
exact model and charged account. If Luna is unavailable or another model is
required, explain why and obtain explicit approval before making that call.
